*  185_pat_cond_assign_defer_seq_minimal.sno -- loop-free reduction of 184.
*  Same defect as 184 (queue row cond-assign-double-fire) with ARBNO, SPAN and
*  digits all removed: two `(epsilon . *f())` sites concatenated, nothing else.
*  Proves the bug is about a SECOND `. *f()` site being reached after the first
*  one already rejected the match -- ARBNO/looping is not required to trigger it.
*  ORACLE PROVENANCE: x64/bin/sbl -bf (correctness oracle, s255 two-oracle ruling).
        DEFINE('mark_fire()')                          :(mark_fire_end)
mark_fire       fire_count = fire_count + 1
        mark_fire = ''                                 :(RETURN)
mark_fire_end
        fire_count = 0
        pattern = (epsilon . *mark_fire()) (epsilon . *mark_fire())
        'X' ? pattern                                  :S(matched)F(no_match)
matched OUTPUT = 'MATCH fire_count=' fire_count        :(END)
no_match        OUTPUT = 'NOMATCH fire_count=' fire_count
END
